0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two builds, selected by the CHECKED line below (CPM is always 0: the 6809
0000                             ;  has no CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: an unchecked build checks nothing)
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build: variables start at 0, words start
0000                             ;                 undefined, and every error in the spec's table stops the
0000                             ;                 program with the four-line report, then goes to EXIT:
0000                             ;                   Err X @ line,col
0000                             ;                   <up to 16 characters of the text at the place>
0000                             ;                   Stk n: ... v v v      (n = depth, then the top 8 values)
0000                             ;                   Rtn n
0000                             ;                 S/s data stack over/underflow, R/r return stack over/
0000                             ;                 underflow, H heap, O store outside the program's space,
0000                             ;                 W bad character after [, U undefined word, Q no closing
0000                             ;                 quote, X reserved byte, Z divide by zero, N unbalanced or
0000                             ;                 mismatched brackets, B Ctrl-C.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In both builds Ctrl-C stops a running program (the unchecked build goes
0000                             ;  to EXIT without a word): see the console layer below for the rules, the
0000                             ;  held key and the break-off cell at 827Bh.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack (S); empty = 8100h. Unchecked: 127 entries.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 112 entries (S down to 8020h); the 32 bytes below
0000                             ;                 are a guard band for what a handler and an interrupt push
0000                             ;                 on top of a full stack before the check runs.
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack (U). Unchecked: 127 cells, empty = 8200h.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 126 cells (U from 81FCh, empty, down to 8100h):
0000                             ;                 the 4 bytes above are a guard band, so a handler that runs
0000                             ;                 on an empty stack writes there and not on the letter
0000                             ;                 cells. A push past the last cell lands on the return
0000                             ;                 stack's bottom entry (80FEh), and the program stops with S
0000                             ;                 before anything reads it.
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh. The break-off
0000                             ;                 cell is at +7Bh (827Bh); +7Ah is free.
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF0Bh  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY) and EXIT are supplied
0000                             ;                 by the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                             ; (the checked startup counts on it being
0000                             ; the page after LETPAGE)
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                COUNT:    EQU   35h   ; the break check's countdown (1 look in 256)
0000                AT:       EQU   36h   ; checked: the address of the character being
0000                             ;   run (big-endian), the place an error reports
0000                PEND:     EQU   38h   ; checked: the program's end, the first byte
0000                             ;   after its NUL (big-endian): the heap's floor
0000                SSAV:     EQU   3Ah   ; checked: S as each character starts (big-
0000                             ;   endian): the return stack an error reports
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   7Bh   ; the break-off cell (827Bh, z9+): 0 = the
0000                             ;   break key is on
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+20h   ; checked: S may go no lower between characters
0000                RSREP:    EQU   RSTOP-16   ; checked: S while the error report runs
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h-4*CHECKED   ; empty data stack (a guard if checked)
0000                DSLIM:    EQU   DSPAGE*256   ; checked: U may go no lower between characters
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Startup
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F004   CE 81 FC               LDU   #DSTOP   
F007   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F009   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F00B                          IF   CHECKED   
F00B                             ; Zero the whole letter page: every variable starts at 0, every word
F00B                             ; cell at 0 (undefined: a call stops with U), and so do the
F00B                             ; interpreter's own cells in the gaps (KEYBUF and the rest). A is
F00B                             ; still LETPAGE; 256 rounds leave X at the next page, PROG.
F00B   5F                     CLRB      
F00C   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   
F00E   6F 80        SZ:       CLR   ,X+   
F010   5A                     DECB      
F011   26 FB                  BNE   sz   
F013                          ENDIF      
F013   10 8E 83 00            LDY   #PROG   ; the reading position
F017                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              CLR   <KEYBUF   ; no key held
                              CLR   <BRKOFF   ; the break key is on
                              TFR   Y,X   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
F017                          ENDIF      
F017   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   
F019   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F01B   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F01D   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F01F   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F021                          IF   CHECKED   
F021   9F 38                  STX   <PEND   ; the heap may never go below this
F023                          ENDIF      
F023                             ; =============================================================================
F023                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F023                             ; 
F023                             ;    00h          end of program
F023                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh       ignored (control, space, DEL)
F023                             ;    80h-FFh      reserved: ignored, or X in the checked build
F023                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F023                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F023                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F023                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F023                             ; =============================================================================
F023                NEXT:        
F023                          IF   CHECKED   
F023                             ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler:
F023                             ; the pointer minus its limit, taken as unsigned, must be no more
F023                             ; than the stack's size. Below the limit (an overflow) it wraps to
F023                             ; FFxxh, and the compare leaves N set; above the empty point (an
F023                             ; underflow) it is just over the size, and N is clear.
F023   30 C9 7F 00            LEAX   (0-DSLIM)&0FFFFh,U   
F027   8C 00 FC               CMPX   #DSTOP-DSLIM   
F02A   22 61                  BHI   e_ds   
F02C   30 E9 7F E0            LEAX   (0-RSLIM)&0FFFFh,S   
F030   8C 00 E0               CMPX   #RSTOP-RSLIM   
F033   22 61                  BHI   e_rs   
F035   10 9F 36               STY   <AT   ; the place, should this character fail
F038   10 DF 3A               STS   <SSAV   ; and the return stack, as it is now
F03B                          ENDIF      
F03B   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F03D   27 72                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F03F   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F041   25 E0                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F043   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F045   25 22                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F047   81 19                  CMPA   #19h   
F049   25 26                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F04B   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F04D   25 18                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h: A = 19h-1Fh
F04F   80 20                  SUBA   #20h   ; A = c - 41h
F051   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F053   25 28                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F055   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F057   25 0C                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F059   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F05B   25 1A                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F05D   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F05F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F05F                          ENDIF      
F05F                          IF   CHECKED   
F05F   27 C2                  BEQ   next   ; 7Fh (DEL): ignored
F061   22 43                  BHI   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
F063                          ENDIF      
F063   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F065   8B 06        P5B:      ADDA   #6   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F067   80 0A        P3A:      SUBA   #0Ah   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F069                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F069   8E F1 1C     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F06C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                                 ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
                                 ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
                              LDB   A,X   
                              CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
                              LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
                              ROLA      
                              JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F06C                          ENDIF      
F06C                          IF   CHECKED   
F06C   48                     ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
F06D   AD 96                  JSR   [A,X]   
F06F                          ENDIF      
F06F   20 B2                  BRA   next   
F071                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F071   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F073   8D 4D                  BSR   rdnum   
F075   20 AC                  BRA   next   
F077                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F077   8D 3B        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F079   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F07B   20 A6                  BRA   next   
F07D                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F07D                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F07D                             ; Checked: a cell still 0 (high byte 0) was never defined, since every
F07D                             ; address in the program's space is 8200h or more. The call has not been
F07D                             ; made yet, so the report shows the stacks as they were.
F07D   8D 35        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F07F   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F081   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F083                          IF   CHECKED   
F083   27 27                  BEQ   e_undef   
F085                          ENDIF      
F085   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F087   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F089   8D 55                  BSR   pollk   ; the break check, at every word call
F08B   20 96                  BRA   next   
F08D                             ; =============================================================================
F08D                             ;  Checked build: the error entries.
F08D                             ; 
F08D                             ;  Each entry loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside a 3-byte
F08D                             ;  CMPX # (the 8Ch), so that a run of them falls through to one place. The
F08D                             ;  place an error reports is the address in AT, which the inner loop sets to
F08D                             ;  each character before it runs it; the one error that reports another
F08D                             ;  place (W, at the character after the [) changes AT before it comes.
F08D                             ; 
F08D                             ;  The report counts the return stack from SSAV, which the inner loop sets
F08D                             ;  to S before each character, so an error may come from any depth of
F08D                             ;  calls: a handler, chkst under one, or ctlc under "?" or the break check.
F08D                             ;  (An r sets SSAV to the empty stack.) The inner loop's own entries are
F08D                             ;  here, where its short branches reach them; those reached from a handler
F08D                             ;  are after h_cstore, just ahead of the report.
F08D                             ; =============================================================================
F08D                          IF   CHECKED   
F08D                             ; ---- reached from the inner loop -------------------------------------------
F08D                             ; The stack checks branch here with N set for an overflow (the pointer is
F08D                             ; below its limit) and clear for an underflow. After an underflow that stack
F08D                             ; counts as empty.
F08D   2B 11        E_DS:     BMI   e_S   
F08F   CE 81 FC               LDU   #DSTOP   ; s
F092   86 73                  LDA   #"s"   
F094   20 18                  BRA   eall   
F096   2B 0B        E_RS:     BMI   e_R   
F098   8E 81 00               LDX   #RSTOP   ; r
F09B   9F 3A                  STX   <SSAV   
F09D   86 72                  LDA   #"r"   
F09F   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0A0   86 53        E_S:      LDA   #"S"   
F0A2   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0A3   86 52        E_R:      LDA   #"R"   
F0A5   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0A6   86 58        E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte (80h-FFh) outside a string
F0A8   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0A9   86 42        E_BREAK:   LDA   #"B"   ; Ctrl-C (from ctlc, at any depth)
F0AB   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0AC   86 55        E_UNDEF:   LDA   #"U"   ; a word never defined (its cell is still 0)
F0AE   7E F3 58     EALL:     JMP   error   
F0B1                          ENDIF      
F0B1   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F0B4                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F0B4   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F0B5   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F0B8   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F0BA   39                     RTS      
F0BB                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F0BB   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F0BD   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F0BF   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F0C1   39           AB9:      RTS      
F0C2                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F0C2                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F0C2                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F0C2   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F0C3   5F                     CLRB      
F0C4   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F0C6   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F0C8   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F0CA   31 21                  LEAY   1,Y   
F0CC   34 02                  PSHS   A   
F0CE   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F0D0   58                     ASLB      
F0D1   49                     ROLA      
F0D2   58                     ASLB      
F0D3   49                     ROLA      
F0D4   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F0D6   58                     ASLB      
F0D7   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F0D8   EB E0                  ADDB   ,S+   
F0DA   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F0DC   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F0DE   20 E6                  BRA   rd1   
F0E0                             ; =============================================================================
F0E0                             ;  Console layer: the break key. A running program reads the keyboard only
F0E0                             ;  through pollk and getk, which between them give the break key its rules:
F0E0                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program;
F0E0                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
F0E0                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
F0E0                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
F0E0                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
F0E0                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
F0E0                             ;  On a break the unchecked build ends without a word (EXIT); the checked
F0E0                             ;  one reports B. All three keep B, X, Y and U.
F0E0                             ; =============================================================================
F0E0                             ; pollk: the break check, at every word call and every true ")" loop-back.
F0E0                             ; It looks at the keyboard only once in 256 calls.
F0E0   0A 35        POLLK:    DEC   <COUNT   
F0E2   26 37                  BNE   cc9   
F0E4   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F0E7   27 32                  BEQ   cc9   ; no key
F0E9   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
F0EB   20 0C                  BRA   ctlc   
F0ED                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 with the zero flag set if there is none.
F0ED   96 34        GETK:     LDA   <KEYBUF   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
F0EF   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   ;   the buffer (it has been through ctlc)
F0F1   4D                     TSTA      
F0F2   26 27                  BNE   cc9   
F0F4   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F0F7   27 22                  BEQ   cc9   
F0F9                             ; ctlc: a key has been read. If it is Ctrl-C and the break key is on, that
F0F9                             ; is the end. If the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one
F0F9                             ; more key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the
F0F9                             ; newest wins), and the Ctrl-C goes on: A = 3, zero flag clear.
F0F9   81 03        CTLC:     CMPA   #3   
F0FB   26 1E                  BNE   cc9   
F0FD   0D 7B                  TST   <BRKOFF   
F0FF   27 A8                  BEQ   brk   
F101   34 10                  PSHS   X   
F103   8E 13 88               LDX   #250*MSLOOP   
F106   BD FF 06     CC1:      JSR   KEY   
F109   26 06                  BNE   cc2   
F10B   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F10D   26 F7                  BNE   cc1   
F10F   20 06                  BRA   cc3   
F111   81 03        CC2:      CMPA   #3   
F113   27 94                  BEQ   brk   
F115   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   
F117   86 03        CC3:      LDA   #3   
F119   35 10                  PULS   X   
F11B   39           CC9:      RTS      
F11C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   fin   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
F11C                          ENDIF      
F11C                          IF   CHECKED   
F11C                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B (the report
F11C                          ENDIF      ;   takes S from SSAV, so the depth of the
F11C                             ;   calls here doesn't matter)
F11C                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F11C                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F11C                             ; return with the carry clear.
F11C                             ; (In the unchecked build it is here, ahead of the table, to leave room in
F11C                             ; the two ranges after it; the checked build has it next to the grave.)
F11C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    HEXC:     BSR   isdig   
                              BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
                              ANDA   #0DFh   
                              SUBA   #11h   
                              CMPA   #6   
                              BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
                              SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
                    HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
                    HV9:      RTS      
F11C                          ENDIF      
F11C                             ; =============================================================================
F11C                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F11C                             ; 
F11C                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F11C                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F11C                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F11C                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F11C                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F11C                             ;  stores a value.)
F11C                             ; 
F11C                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F11C                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F11C                             ; =============================================================================
F11C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
                    PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
                    PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
                    PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
                    PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
                    NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F11C                          ENDIF      
F11C                PTAB:        
F11C                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
                              FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
                              FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
                              FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
                              FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
                              FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
                              FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
                              FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
                              FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
                              FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
                              FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
                              FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
                              FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
                              FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
                              FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
                              FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
                              FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
                              FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
                              FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
                              FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
                              FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
                              FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
                              FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
                              FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
                              FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
                              FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
                              FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
                              FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
                              FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
                              FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
                              FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
                              FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F11C                          ENDIF      
F11C                          IF   CHECKED   
F11C   F3 2E                  FDB   h_store   ; !
F11E   F2 3A                  FDB   h_str   ; "
F120   F4 22                  FDB   h_num   ; #
F122   F3 15                  FDB   h_print   ; $
F124   F3 01                  FDB   h_swap   ; %
F126   F4 47                  FDB   h_and   ; &
F128   F3 0D                  FDB   h_emit   ; '
F12A   F2 AB                  FDB   h_open   ; (
F12C   F2 BF                  FDB   h_close   ; )
F12E   F2 CB                  FDB   h_mul   ; *
F130   F4 4F                  FDB   h_add   ; +
F132   F2 B7                  FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
F134   F4 56                  FDB   h_sub   ; -
F136   F3 3A                  FDB   h_cstore   ; .
F138   F4 61                  FDB   h_div   ; /
F13A   F3 08                  FDB   h_dup   ; :
F13C   F3 12                  FDB   h_drop   ; ;
F13E   F2 E9                  FDB   h_lt   ; <
F140   F2 F5                  FDB   h_eq   ; =
F142   F2 E7                  FDB   h_gt   ; >
F144   F2 5D                  FDB   h_key   ; ?
F146   F2 57                  FDB   h_fetch   ; @
F148   F1 F1                  FDB   h_def   ; [
F14A   F1 D2                  FDB   h_break   ; \
F14C   F1 CE                  FDB   h_ret   ; ]
F14E   F1 64                  FDB   h_xor   ; ^
F150   F1 80                  FDB   h_alloc   ; _
F152   F1 9C                  FDB   h_grave   ; `
F154   F1 72                  FDB   h_tor   ; {
F156   F1 5C                  FDB   h_or   ; |
F158   F1 7A                  FDB   h_fromr   ; }
F15A   F1 6D                  FDB   h_not   ; ~
F15C                          ENDIF      
F15C                PTABEND:      
F15C                             ; =============================================================================
F15C                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F15C                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F15C                             ; =============================================================================
F15C   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F15E   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F160   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F162   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F164   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F166   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F168   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F16A   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F16C   39                     RTS      
F16D   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F16F   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F171   39                     RTS      
F172                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F172                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F172   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F174   37 06                  PULU   D   
F176   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F178   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F17A                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )    The dispatcher's return address comes off
F17A                             ; into D and the entry under it into X; D is then jumped to.
F17A   35 16        H_FROMR:   PULS   D,X   
F17C   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F17E   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   
F180                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n (signed: a 16-bit add);
F180                             ; TOS is the old pointer.
F180                             ; Checked: the new top must be at least the program's end (PEND) and below
F180                             ; the limit page. That also catches an add that wraps: the top is always
F180                             ; 8301h-EFFFh and n is -32768..32767, so a sum that carries past FFFFh
F180                             ; lands below 7000h, and one that borrows can't happen.
F180   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F182   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F184   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F186   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F188                          IF   CHECKED   
F188   10 93 38               CMPD   <PEND   
F18B   25 04                  BLO   ah9   ; below the program's end
F18D   81 F0                  CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
F18F   25 04                  BLO   ah1   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
F191   86 48        AH9:      LDA   #"H"   
F193   20 59                  BRA   ejmp   ; (with [ below)
F195                AH1:         
F195                          ENDIF      
F195   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F197   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F199   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F19B   39                     RTS      
F19C                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
F19C                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
F19C                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS (39h) is
F19C                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
F19C                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
F19C                             ; code is entered by JSR (the dispatcher's own), with the address already
F19C                             ; popped: U points at the top data cell (big-endian, 2 bytes, stack grows
F19C                             ; down) and the return address is on top of S. The code may pop and push
F19C                             ; data cells by changing U; on return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F19C                             ; keep Y (the interpreter's reading position), DP and S (balanced), and
F19C                             ; return with RTS. A, B, X, CC may change.
F19C                             ; Neither the loader's stores nor the code are checked, in either build.
F19C   8D 1E        H_GRAVE:   BSR   hexc   ; the digit after the grave, if any
F19E   24 1A                  BCC   exec   
F1A0   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   
F1A2   C6 10        HX1:      LDB   #16   
F1A4   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F1A5   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F1A7   8D 13                  BSR   hexc   
F1A9   24 08                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F1AB   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F1AD   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F1AF   8D 0B                  BSR   hexc   
F1B1   25 EF                  BCS   hx1   
F1B3   86 39        HX2:      LDA   #39h   ; RTS
F1B5   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F1B7   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F1B9   39                     RTS      
F1BA   37 80        EXEC:     PULU   PC   ; jump to it: the code's RTS returns to the
F1BC                             ;   dispatcher
F1BC                          IF   CHECKED   
F1BC   BD F0 BB     HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
F1BF   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F1C1   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F1C3   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F1C5   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F1C7   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F1C9   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F1CB   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F1CD   39           HV9:      RTS      
F1CE                          ENDIF      
F1CE                             ; ---- where the two ranges meet ---------------------------------------------
F1CE                             ; The first range ends somewhere among the next five handlers, ] \ [ @ ?
F1CE                             ; (they are in falling code order for this): NPG1 follows. Every handler
F1CE                             ; below them must start in the second range, and every one above in the
F1CE                             ; first.
F1CE                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. (PULS X,Y: the dispatcher's
F1CE                             ; return address into X, then the saved IP into Y.)
F1CE   35 30        H_RET:    PULS   X,Y   
F1D0   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F1D2                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
F1D2                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
F1D2   EC C1        H_BREAK:   LDD   ,U++   
F1D4   27 60                  BEQ   sk9   ; false: nothing to do
F1D6   8D 3F                  BSR   skip   
F1D8   4D                     TSTA      ; skip returns 0 for ")"
F1D9                          IF   CHECKED   
F1D9   10 2B FE D4            LBMI   fin   ; (and FFh for the NUL: the program ends)
F1DD                          ENDIF      
F1DD   26 EF                  BNE   h_ret   
F1DF   35 16        RDROP:    PULS   D,X   ; the return address and the block start
F1E1   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   ; back to the dispatcher
F1E3                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
F1E3                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
F1E3                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
F1E3                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
F1E3                             ; checked build stops on it.)
F1E3                          IF   CHECKED   
F1E3   81 DF        DEF1:     CMPA   #" "-"A"+256   
F1E5   27 20                  BEQ   def2   
F1E7   31 3F                  LEAY   -1,Y   ; anything but a letter or a space: W. The
F1E9   10 9F 36               STY   <AT   ;   place is that character, just read
F1EC   86 57                  LDA   #"W"   
F1EE   7E F3 58     EJMP:     JMP   error   ; (H and N come here too)
F1F1                          ENDIF      
F1F1   A6 A0        H_DEF:    LDA   ,Y+   
F1F3   80 41                  SUBA   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
F1F5   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ;   lands 64 bytes up
F1F7   C4 DF                  ANDB   #0DFh   ; fold case
F1F9   C1 1A                  CMPB   #26   
F1FB                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BHS   def2   ; not a letter
F1FB                          ENDIF      
F1FB                          IF   CHECKED   
F1FB   24 E6                  BHS   def1   
F1FD                          ENDIF      
F1FD   BD F0 B4               JSR   cellx   
F200   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F202   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; little-endian
F204   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F206   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PSHU)
F207   36 20        DEF2:     PSHU   Y   ; an anonymous block: push its address
F209                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                                 ; fall into skip
F209                          ENDIF      
F209                          IF   CHECKED   
F209                             ; Checked: the skip must end at a "]" (A = 2), or for a false "(",
F209                             ; which comes to opf, at a ")" (A = 0). Anything else stops with N.
F209   8D 0C                  BSR   skip   
F20B   80 02                  SUBA   #2   
F20D   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the BSR)
F20E   8D 07        OPF:      BSR   skip   
F210   4D                     TSTA      
F211   27 23                  BEQ   sk9   ; (an RTS)
F213   86 4E                  LDA   #"N"   
F215   20 D7                  BRA   ejmp   
F217                          ENDIF      
F217                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
F217                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
F217                             ; strings are stepped over whole. B counts the open levels.
F217                             ; Unchecked: a NUL first ends the program (for "\" with no closer; anything
F217                             ; else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets anyway).
F217                             ; Checked: a NUL, or a string that runs into it, returns A = FFh, and the
F217                             ; caller decides: "\" ends the program, "(" and "[" stop with N, as they do
F217                             ; for a closer of the other kind. The place is the opener, still in AT.
F217   5F           SKIP:     CLRB      
F218   A6 A0        SK1:      LDA   ,Y+   
F21A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   fin   
F21A                          ENDIF      
F21A                          IF   CHECKED   
F21A   27 38                  BEQ   ssn   ; A = FFh
F21C                          ENDIF      
F21C   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F21E   26 04                  BNE   sk2   
F220   8D 25                  BSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
F222                          IF   CHECKED   
F222   25 12                  BCS   sk9   ; (or FFh, with the carry set: unclosed)
F224                          ENDIF      
F224   80 28        SK2:      SUBA   #"("   
F226   27 0F                  BEQ   sk3   
F228   4A                     DECA      ; ")"
F229   27 08                  BEQ   sk4   
F22B   80 32                  SUBA   #"["-")"   
F22D   27 08                  BEQ   sk3   
F22F   81 02                  CMPA   #"]"-"["   
F231   26 E5                  BNE   sk1   
F233   5A           SK4:      DECB      
F234   2A E2                  BPL   sk1   
F236   39           SK9:      RTS      ; the closer at this level
F237   5C           SK3:      INCB      
F238   20 DE                  BRA   sk1   
F23A                             ; 22h, checked build (the unchecked one is with the handlers below).
F23A                             ; Checked: a NUL ends the string too, even right after a "/"; skipstr then
F23A                             ; returns A = FFh with the carry set (the carry is clear at the quote), and
F23A                             ; """ stops with Q, the string's address already pushed. (skip comes here
F23A                             ; for its own NUL as well.)
F23A                          IF   CHECKED   
F23A   36 20        H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
F23C   8D 09                  BSR   skipstr   
F23E   10 25 01 14            LBCS   e_quote   
F242   39                     RTS      
F243   A6 A0        SS0:      LDA   ,Y+   ; the character after the "/"
F245   27 0D                  BEQ   ssn   
F247   A6 A0        SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
F249   27 09                  BEQ   ssn   
F24B   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F24D   27 F4                  BEQ   ss0   
F24F   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F251   26 F4                  BNE   skipstr   
F253   39                     RTS      ; the quote: C = 0
F254   80 01        SSN:      SUBA   #1   ; the NUL: A = FFh, C = 1
F256   39                     RTS      
F257                          ENDIF      
F257   AE C4        H_FETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; "@" (the cell in memory is little-endian)
F259   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F25B   20 5D                  BRA   cf1   
F25D                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
F25D                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
F25D                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
F25D                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
F25D                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
F25D   AE C4        H_KEY:    LDX   ,U   
F25F   2B 17                  BMI   line   
F261   C6 14        KT1:      LDB   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
F263   BD F0 ED     KT2:      JSR   getk   
F266   26 0B                  BNE   kt3   
F268   5A                     DECB      
F269   26 F8                  BNE   kt2   
F26B   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F26D   26 F2                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
F26F   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   ; 0?: the countdown from 0 took 65536 ms;
F271   27 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ;   run it again, until a key comes
F273   6F C4        KT3:      CLR   ,U   
F275   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F277   39                     RTS      
F278                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
F278                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
F278                             ; is full. B = the length so far; the low byte of the top cell becomes the
F278                             ; most allowed (it holds minus the count on entry).
F278   8C FF 81     LINE:     CMPX   #-127   ; (X = TOS, minus the count)
F27B   24 04                  BHS   ln1   
F27D   86 81                  LDA   #-127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
F27F   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F281   60 41        LN1:      NEG   1,U   
F283   8E 82 80               LDX   #LINEBUF   
F286   5F                     CLRB      
F287   BD F0 ED     LN2:      JSR   getk   
F28A   27 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
F28C   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F28E   27 16                  BEQ   ln5   
F290   81 08                  CMPA   #8   
F292   27 0C                  BEQ   ln4   
F294   E1 41                  CMPB   1,U   
F296   24 EF                  BHS   ln2   ; full
F298   A7 85                  STA   B,X   
F29A   5C                     INCB      
F29B   BD FF 03     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
F29E   20 E7                  BRA   ln2   
F2A0   5D           LN4:      TSTB      ; Backspace: nothing to take back?
F2A1   27 E4                  BEQ   ln2   
F2A3   5A                     DECB      
F2A4   20 F5                  BRA   ln3   ; echo it
F2A6   A7 85        LN5:      STA   B,X   ; A = 13
F2A8   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F2AA   39                     RTS      
F2AB                             ; =============================================================================
F2AB                             ;  Handlers that must start in the second range (unchecked build).
F2AB                             ; =============================================================================
F2AB                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
F2AB                             ; the matching ")".
F2AB   EC C1        H_OPEN:   LDD   ,U++   
F2AD                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   skip   ; tail call: skip ends in RTS
F2AD                          ENDIF      
F2AD                          IF   CHECKED   
F2AD   10 27 FF 5D            LBEQ   opf   ; checked: skip, and check the closer
F2B1                          ENDIF      
F2B1   35 10                  PULS   X   
F2B3   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F2B5   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F2B7                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
F2B7                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
F2B7                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h. (The checked
F2B7                             ; build's is after skip.)
F2B7                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAY)
                    SS0:      LEAY   1,Y   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
                              CMPA   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMPA   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      
F2B7                          ENDIF      
F2B7   AE C4        H_CFETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; ","
F2B9   4F                     CLRA      
F2BA   E6 84        CF1:      LDB   ,X   
F2BC   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F2BE   39                     RTS      
F2BF                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
F2BF                             ; drops it and carries on.
F2BF   EC C1        H_CLOSE:   LDD   ,U++   
F2C1   10 27 FF 1A            LBEQ   rdrop   
F2C5   10 AE 62               LDY   2,S   ; the block start, under the return address
F2C8   7E F0 E0               JMP   pollk   ; the break check, at every loop-back
F2CB                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
F2CB                             ; "*": three 8x8 multiplies; only the low 16 bits are kept.
F2CB                             ; a = ah:al at 2,U.  b = bh:bl at ,U.
F2CB   A6 43        H_MUL:    LDA   3,U   
F2CD   E6 C4                  LDB   ,U   
F2CF   3D                     MUL      ; al*bh
F2D0   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; (bh is no longer needed)
F2D2   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F2D4   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F2D6   3D                     MUL      ; ah*bl
F2D7   EB C4                  ADDB   ,U   
F2D9   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; the cross terms, low byte
F2DB   A6 43                  LDA   3,U   
F2DD   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F2DF   3D                     MUL      ; al*bl
F2E0   AB C4                  ADDA   ,U   
F2E2   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F2E4   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F2E6   39                     RTS      
F2E7                             ; Signed compares: a-b, then a branch to put -1 or 0 on the stack.
F2E7   8D 18        H_GT:     BSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
F2E9   8D 10        H_LT:     BSR   cmp   
F2EB   2D 02                  BLT   true   
F2ED   5F           FALSE:    CLRB      
F2EE   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F2EF   C6 FF        TRUE:     LDB   #0FFh   
F2F1   1D                     SEX      ; D = 0000 or FFFF
F2F2   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F2F4   39                     RTS      
F2F5   8D 04        H_EQ:     BSR   cmp   
F2F7   27 F6                  BEQ   true   
F2F9   20 F2                  BRA   false   
F2FB   EC 42        CMP:      LDD   2,U   
F2FD   10 A3 C1               CMPD   ,U++   
F300   39                     RTS      
F301                             ; ---- stack, and printing ----------------------------------------------------
F301   37 16        H_SWAP:   PULU   D,X   ; "%"
F303   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F305   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F307   39                     RTS      
F308   EC C4        H_DUP:    LDD   ,U   ; ":"
F30A   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F30C   39                     RTS      
F30D   A6 41        H_EMIT:   LDA   1,U   ; "'"
F30F                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BSR   putc   
F30F                          ENDIF      
F30F                          IF   CHECKED   
F30F   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   ; (the checked build's report is in the way)
F312                          ENDIF      
F312   33 42        H_DROP:   LEAU   2,U   ; ";"
F314   39                     RTS      
F315                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
F315                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
F315                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
F315                             ; Checked: a NUL (not one escaped by "/") stops with Q, the string's address
F315                             ; still on the stack.
F315   AE C4        H_PRINT:   LDX   ,U   
F317   A6 80        PR0:      LDA   ,X+   
F319                          IF   CHECKED   
F319   10 27 00 39            LBEQ   e_quote   
F31D                          ENDIF      
F31D   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F31F   27 F1                  BEQ   h_drop   
F321   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F323   26 04                  BNE   pr1   
F325   A6 80                  LDA   ,X+   
F327   84 BF                  ANDA   #0BFh   
F329                PR1:         
F329                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BSR   putc   
F329                          ENDIF      
F329                          IF   CHECKED   
F329   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F32C                          ENDIF      
F32C   20 E9                  BRA   pr0   
F32E                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." with the high byte stored first. The cell in
F32E                             ; memory is little-endian.
F32E                             ; Checked: both bytes must be in the program's space, and they are tested
F32E                             ; before either is stored (chkst stops with O, the stack untouched).
F32E   AE C4        H_STORE:   LDX   ,U   
F330                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              LDA   2,U   
                              STA   1,X   
F330                          ENDIF      
F330                          IF   CHECKED   
F330   8D 13                  BSR   chkst   
F332   30 01                  LEAX   1,X   
F334   8D 0F                  BSR   chkst   
F336   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F338   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F33A                             ; and fall into ".", which loads X again (and checks it again)
F33A                          ENDIF      
F33A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDX)
F33A                          ENDIF      
F33A   AE C4        H_CSTORE:   LDX   ,U   ; "." ( c addr -- )
F33C                          IF   CHECKED   
F33C   8D 07                  BSR   chkst   
F33E                          ENDIF      
F33E   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F340   37 06                  PULU   D   
F342   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F344   39                     RTS      
F345                          IF   CHECKED   
F345                             ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
F345                             ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
F345                             ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
F345                             ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
F345                             ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
F345   8C 82 00     CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
F348   25 06                  BLO   cs9   
F34A   8C F0 00               CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
F34D   24 01                  BHS   cs9   
F34F   39                     RTS      ; in range
F350   86 4F        CS9:      LDA   #"O"   
F352   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F353   86 5A        E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; / by zero
F355   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F356   86 51        E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; " or $ ran into the NUL
F358                             ; and fall into error. (H, W and N have their own entries, near
F358                             ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
F358                             ; =============================================================================
F358                             ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
F358                             ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
F358                             ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
F358                             ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
F358                             ;  short calls. Prints
F358                             ; 
F358                             ;     CR LF
F358                             ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
F358                             ;     <up to 16 raw characters from the place, ending early at CR, LF, NUL>
F358                             ;     CR LF
F358                             ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
F358                             ;     Rtn n CR LF
F358                             ; 
F358                             ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
F358                             ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
F358                             ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
F358                             ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
F358                             ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
F358                             ; 
F358                             ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
F358                             ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
F358                             ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
F358                             ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
F358                             ; =============================================================================
F358   10 CE 80 F0  ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
F35C   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
F35E   8D 34                  BSR   pmsg   
F360   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0      FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
F366   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
F368   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F36B   8D 27                  BSR   pmsg   
F36D   20 40 A0               FCB   " @"," "+80h   
F370                             ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
F370                             ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
F370   10 8E 00 00            LDY   #0   
F374   8E 82 7F               LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
F377   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F379   8E 82 FF               LDX   #PROG-1   
F37C   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F37E   24 23                  BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
F380   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F382   31 21        LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
F384   30 01        LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
F386   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F388   24 19                  BHS   lc3   
F38A   A6 84                  LDA   ,X   
F38C   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F38E   26 F4                  BNE   lc2   
F390   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F392   20 EE                  BRA   lc1   
F394                             ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
F394                             ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
F394                             ; (It sits here, in the middle of the report, where all its calls reach.)
F394   35 10        PMSG:     PULS   X   
F396   A6 84        PM1:      LDA   ,X   
F398   84 7F                  ANDA   #7Fh   
F39A   BD F4 44               JSR   putc   
F39D   6D 80                  TST   ,X+   
F39F   2A F5                  BPL   pm1   
F3A1   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F3A3   DC 36        LC3:      LDD   <AT   
F3A5   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F3A7   ED C4                  STD   ,U   ; the column
F3A9   36 20                  PSHU   Y   
F3AB   BD F4 2C               JSR   pdec   ; the line
F3AE   8D E4                  BSR   pmsg   
F3B0   AC                     FCB   ","+80h   
F3B1   8D 79                  BSR   pdec   ; the column
F3B3   8D DF                  BSR   pmsg   
F3B5   0D 8A                  FCB   13,10+80h   
F3B7                             ; the text at the place
F3B7   9E 36                  LDX   <AT   
F3B9   C6 10                  LDB   #16   
F3BB   A6 80        TX1:      LDA   ,X+   
F3BD   27 0D                  BEQ   tx9   
F3BF   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F3C1   27 09                  BEQ   tx9   
F3C3   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F3C5   27 05                  BEQ   tx9   
F3C7   8D 7B                  BSR   putc   
F3C9   5A                     DECB      
F3CA   26 EF                  BNE   tx1   
F3CC   8D C6        TX9:      BSR   pmsg   
F3CE   0D 0A 53 74 6B A0      FCB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
F3D4                             ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
F3D4                             ; the program's top cell, at ,U.
F3D4   34 40                  PSHS   U   ; where the walk ends
F3D6   CC 81 FC               LDD   #DSTOP   
F3D9   A3 E4                  SUBD   ,S   
F3DB   8D 3F                  BSR   pdh   ; the depth (pdec leaves U as it was)
F3DD   8D B5                  BSR   pmsg   
F3DF   BA                     FCB   ":"+80h   
F3E0   31 C8 10               LEAY   16,U   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
F3E3   10 8C 81 FC            CMPY   #DSTOP   
F3E7   24 08                  BHS   sl1   
F3E9   8D A9                  BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
F3EB   20 2E 2E AE            FCB   " ..","."+80h   
F3EF   20 04                  BRA   sl2   
F3F1   10 8E 81 FC  SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
F3F5   10 AC E4     SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
F3F8   23 0B                  BLS   sl9   
F3FA   EC A3                  LDD   ,--Y   
F3FC   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3FE   8D 94                  BSR   pmsg   
F400   A0                     FCB   " "+80h   
F401   8D 1F                  BSR   h_num   
F403   20 F0                  BRA   sl2   
F405   8D 8D        SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
F407   0D 0A 52 74 6E A0      FCB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
F40D   CC 81 00               LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
F410   93 3A                  SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
F412   8D 08                  BSR   pdh   
F414   BD F3 94               JSR   pmsg   
F417   0D 8A                  FCB   13,10+80h   
F419   7E FF 09               JMP   EXIT   
F41C                             ; pdh: print D/2 (a depth: D is twice it), unsigned.
F41C   44           PDH:      LSRA      
F41D   56                     RORB      
F41E   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F420   20 0A                  BRA   pdec   
F422                          ENDIF      
F422                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F422   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F424   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F426   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F428   8D 1A                  BSR   putc   
F42A   8D 5E                  BSR   negt   
F42C                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F42C   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F42F   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F431   8D 68                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F433   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F435   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F437   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F439   27 03                  BEQ   pd1   
F43B   8D EF                  BSR   pdec   ; (it drops the quotient)
F43D   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAU)
F43E   33 42        PD1:      LEAU   2,U   ; drop the zero quotient
F440   35 02                  PULS   A   
F442   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F444   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F447                             ; ---- more arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------------
F447   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F449   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F44B   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F44D   20 04                  BRA   st   
F44F   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F451   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F453   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F455   39                     RTS      
F456                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F456   BD F0 BB     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F459   25 2C                  BLO   negnum   
F45B   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F45D   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F45F   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F461                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F461                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F461                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F461                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F461                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F461                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F461                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F461                H_DIV:       
F461                          IF   CHECKED   
F461   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F463   10 27 FE EC            LBEQ   e_zero   
F467                          ENDIF      
F467   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F469   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F46B   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F46D   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F46F   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F471   8D 22                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F473   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F475   8D 1E                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F477   8D 22                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F479   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F47B   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F47D   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F47F   8D 0B                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F481   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F483   2A 0F                  BPL   ng9   
F485   20 03                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F487   BD F0 C2     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F48A   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F48C   EC 84        NEGX:     LDD   ,X   ; negx: negate the cell at X
F48E   40                     NEGA      
F48F   50                     NEGB      
F490   82 00                  SBCA   #0   
F492   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F494   39           NG9:      RTS      
F495   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F497   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F499   20 F1                  BRA   negx   
F49B                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F49B                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F49B                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F49B                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F49B                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
F49B   EC C4        UDIV:     LDD   ,U   
F49D   83 00 02               SUBD   #2   
F4A0   26 07                  BNE   ud0   
F4A2   64 42                  LSR   2,U   
F4A4   66 43                  ROR   3,U   ; the quotient
F4A6   59                     ROLB      ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D was 0)
F4A7   20 18                  BRA   ud3   
F4A9   8E 00 10     UD0:      LDX   #16   
F4AC   4F                     CLRA      
F4AD   5F                     CLRB      
F4AE   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F4B0   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F4B2   59                     ROLB      
F4B3   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F4B4   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F4B7   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F4B9   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F4BB   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F4BD   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F4BF   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F4C1   ED C4        UD3:      STD   ,U   
F4C3   39                     RTS      
F4C4                IMGEND:      


